:: Ben 5-Mile Jog [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 5>>
You are idling around in your front yard, waving around a fallen branch that you found on the ground as cars pass by your house at an average rate despite the street ending in a cul-de-sac. You came out here to do something, but for one reason or another, you’ve become completely distracted and now just stand there entertaining yourself in senseless ways. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on boy! One-Two-Three-Four! Come on, speed up! We’re almost at our halfway point!”</span> A voice shouts out sounding like the military drill instructors you see in the movies. You glance upwards and see a familiar looking muscular man jogging down the street wearing shorts and a tank top. <br>

<<if $Player.Kinks.Adult == 1>>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: Pink">The man is ripped, built like a Greek statue with muscles that shine from the sweat reflecting off the sun. Your mind instantly begins to mentally undress the chiseled form of the man, but you pause upon realizing you’ve seen this man before.</span> <br>
<</if>>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Ben",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Exercise",
            Eyes: "Sad",
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Blush: 2,
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

/* Ben: (Custom Outfit) */
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Wa- wait! Hold on- I’m… Aaahhhhh!”</span> An exhausted, pitiful wail comes from further down the street. You turn and, to your surprise, see your classmate and friend <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> stumbling down the street in the most pathetic attempt of a run you’ve ever witnessed. He looks like a mix of a toddler just learning to walk and a puppet being controlled by strings on some educational children’s show. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I… Bleh…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> makes it right to your mailbox before collapsing to the ground in front of his still jogging-in-place father. He rolls onto his back and stares up at the sky, breathing deeply and absolutely drenched in sweat. You’ve never seen a boy looking so utterly exhausted in your life. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… I think my lungs exploded.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nonsense.”</span> His father laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s just your body getting used to it. Last weekend you only made it to the street corner, so this is what I call progress! Now come on, we’re just got to do a few laps around the soccer field, and we can head home! Hut, one-two-three-four!”</span> The man returns to his drill sergeant voice, trying to coerce an utterly drained <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> back to his feet to continue running. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t… think… I… can move…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> says between deep breaths, closing his eyes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Just… leave me here… to die…! Please!”</span> He whines, splayed out on the sidewalk like roadkill. Neither one of them seems to have noticed you staring just a few feet away. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Benjamin</span>…”</span> His father sighs deeply, finally stopping his jog, but then immediately stretches his arms out to keep his heartrate up. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You’ll never learn to stand up for yourself if you can’t handle a little 5-mile jog. This is nothing, back on base we used to do twice this much every day before breakfast! The army doesn’t take no quitters and neither do the <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Fischer’s</span>!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well maybe I’m not cut out for the army.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> mumbles under his breath, sounding equally annoyed as he does exhausted. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nonsense! Never been a <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Fischer</span> who hasn’t, it’s in your blood. You just need to apply yourself. Books are fine and dandy for school, but in the real world it’s stuff like this that-”</span>  He pauses, sighing once more, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alrighty soldier, I can see when you’ve hit your limit. Good hustle though, like I said you’ve done much better than last weekend! Tell you what, take a minute to catch your breath. I’ll do the laps around the field then come grab you. Then it’s just a short 3-quarter mile back home!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> groans loudly, some sobbing sneaking through as his father chuckles and continues on jogging. <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Make yourself known<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Someone please kill me…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> says once his father is far enough away. You chuckle, finally making your presence known, and say the best you can do is maim him, since <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Your Father</span> won’t let you drive the car. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$BenNickname</span>!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> <span style="Color: Pink">snaps his head up in surprise, his already red face turning pinker.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Wha… wha… where did you…? You didn’t…?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> mumbles out before exhaling and lying his head back on the ground. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, I’m too tired to be embarrassed. Just run me over, please. I promise not to haunt you.”</span> 

        <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Ben",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Exercise",
                Eyes: "Sad",
                Mouth: "Happy",
                Blush: 2,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

        You laugh and help <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> up, who is so utterly exhausted he can’t move a single muscle. You carry the surprisingly light boy to your porch under the shade and go inside and get him some water. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s energy returns the instant he sees the cool liquid, and he gulps it down like he has been stuck in a desert for a week. He exhales loudly with pleasure as he finishes, placing the cup down, before once again collapsing back onto the porch. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you. Now, I can die in peace…”</span> He says, closing his eyes. You chuckle and elbow him playfully. The boy groans, very sore, and you apologize. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine… I already hurt all over…”</span> A bit worried, you ask him what’s going on. You don’t take him for the exercise type, no offense. Does his father use exercise as a punishment or something? <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yes, but that’s not what this is about.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> sits up, groaning in pain and rubbing his shoulder as he does so. Still unable to sit up straight, he leans against the railing and sighs loudly. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll tell you, but promise you won’t make fun of me?”</span> He says, <span style="Color: LightCoral">looking at you like a puppy that was just kicked.</span> You nod. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“A few weeks ago, some older kids cornered me in the park and… beat me up.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">He says that last part quietly, obviously a little embarrassed.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Stole the money I had on me and gave me a black eye. Normally it wouldn’t be a big deal, I’d just say I tripped or something, but mom didn’t believe me and well…”</span> He sighs, slumping down in defeat. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now dad is trying to ‘toughen me up’ by bringing me on his morning runs. This is the third weekend in a row. He seems to think the solution to violence is me fighting back, for some reason! I had to spend all afternoon in bed recovering last weekend. At this rate, I’ll be dead by the end of the month.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> once again collapses onto the porch, sighing in defeat. 

        <<set _ad to [
        {
