                <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You don’t get it. Progress in my family doesn’t mean back down, it means up the challenge.”</span> He sighs loudly, pressing his hands into his face, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But I guess that’s my only choice. Thanks anyway.”</span> He gives you a pitiful smile before slowly standing up, groaning in pain the entire time. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Just promise you’ll say nice things at my funeral, someone has to.”</span> You smile and assure him that others will say nice things too, though <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> doesn’t seem too sure. <br>
                <br>
                <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s dad returns a moment later, jogging along with his military cadence and rhythm. He calls out to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> as he approaches your house and the boy, sighing loudly and groaning as he tries to jog more, follows behind him. <span style="Color: Yellow">You give him a pitiful wave and smile as he disappears down the street, looking like he may pass out at any moment.</span> <br>
