            <<replace"#choice2">>
                You tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> that he should tell his dad how he feels. If he explains that he needs a break or for some lighter exercise, you’re sure his dad will listen. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> gives you a look that tells you that it would be the exact opposite. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Trying to explain feelings to my dad is like trying to explain algebra to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>.”</span> You smile at the comparison, but don’t fully get what he means. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He doesn’t understand how numbers and letter go together! They may be different, but both can work with the other! It’s just algebra!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> says as if it is the most obvious thing in the world, though you are still a little confused. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> sighs loudly, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Never mind.”</span> 
              
