                As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s father’s voice returns, the military cadence breaking through the quiet of the neighborhood, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> slumps down in utter exhaustion before forcing himself back to his feet. He groans in pain with every step as he limps back towards the sidewalk as his dad, looking to be even more energized, comes into view. You encourage your friend to say something and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>, looking exhausted enough to give anything a try, freezes in place and opens his mouth to speak. <span style="Color: Pink">However, much to your amusement, only a bumbled mess of words come out.</span> <br>
                <br>
                <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What are you doing?”</span> His father asks, confused at the utter word vomit that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> produced. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> tries to speak once more, <span style="Color: Pink">before turning bright red out of embarrassment and slumping his arms down in defeat.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>? Are you feeling too hot? You’re bright red! Here, take off your shirt. It’ll cool you down-”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">His father reaches down and grips the bottom of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s shirt, yanking it upwards. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> cries out in embarrassment as his pale, scrawny chest is exposed. You can’t help but smiles at the sight of his swetty belly and the waistband of his tighty whities poking out as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> flails about to get his shirt back down.</span>
                
