                <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Please… stop…”</span> He sounds desperate, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t need work out tips! That’s all my dad does, that’s all my brother does, that’s all my grandpa does! I don’t need you, of all people, to join them. What I NEED is for someone to explain to my family that I’m not a fighter; I’m just a nerdy little weakling and they need to understand that!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> groans once more, rolling into a fetal position, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry. It’s not your fault, you’re just trying to help, It’s just…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine. I’m just tired and sore and… tired…”</span> <br>
                <br>
                <span style="Color: LightCoral">You feel a little bad, apologizing, but that just makes <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> feel worse.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now I feel like a jerk for blowing up on you.”</span> You smile; <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s quiet little rant is the furthest thing from a ‘blow-up’. He can vent to you whenever he wants, that’s what friends are for. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> smiles at this, sitting up slowly. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks. That kind of help I’m happy to have.”</span> The tender moment is interrupted by <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span>’s dad, his military chanting breaking through the quietness of the neighborhood. <span style="Color: Yellow"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Ben</span> sighs one final time upon hearing it, slowly standing up and thanking you once more before heading off to continue his torturous jog. You wish him luck.</span> <br>
